Description: htop/btop for Odoo -- terminal monitor for Odoo servers
 otop is a compact terminal monitor for servers running Odoo. It shows, side by
 side for as many instances as are configured (LIVE, STAGING, ...):
 .
  * CPU, per-core load, RAM, swap, load average, disk I/O and network
  * Odoo worker processes: pid, CPU, memory, uptime and busy/idle state
  * total disk usage first, then PostgreSQL database, Odoo filestore and other
  * PostgreSQL connections, active/idle/waiting backends, long queries
 .
 Worker busy/idle comes from observable evidence -- an established
 connection on the Odoo HTTP port or an active database query -- not from
 CPU usage, and anything approximated is labelled as such.
 .
 It runs as a single process with no daemon, no web server and no external
 services, and reads its configuration from /etc/otop/config.yaml.

